{"read":"2026-11-11","county":"Osceola County, Florida","source":"Osceola County Supervisor of Elections — official sample ballot for every precinct (Nov 3, 2026 General Election, “Sample Ballots by Precinct”)","sourceUrl":"https://www.voteosceola.gov/en-us/sampleballots/","lookup":"https://www.voteosceola.gov/en-us/","office":"Osceola County Supervisor of Elections","c":[{"t":"r","title":"United States Senator","d":"","vf":"1","c":[["Ashley Moody","Republican"],["Angie Nixon","Democratic"],["Neil J. Gillespie","No Party Affiliation"]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"Representative in Congress","d":"District 18","vf":"1","c":[["Scott Franklin","Republican"],["Curtis Gibson","Democratic"],["Deva Simmons","No Party Affiliation"]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"Governor and Lieutenant Governor","d":"","vf":"1","c":[["Byron Donalds and Bryan Avila","Republican"],["David Jolly and Gwen Graham","Democratic"],["Scott Eckhard Jewett and Nicole Skelly","Libertarian"],["Charles Burkett and Ruben A. Coto","No Party Affiliation"],["Frank J. Russo and Rachel Rodriguez","No Party Affiliation"],["Moliere \"Moe\" Dimanche and Benjiman Rojas","No Party Affiliation"],["Dean Ocean Abrams and Joe Van Vactor","No Party Affiliation"],["Jeffrey Peter \"Dr. Jeff\" Datto and Juan Santana","No Party Affiliation"]],"wi":1,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"Attorney General","d":"","vf":"1","c":[["James Uthmeier","Republican"],["Jose Javier Rodriguez","Democratic"]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"Chief Financial Officer","d":"","vf":"1","c":[["Blaise Ingoglia","Republican"],["Annette Taddeo","Democratic"]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"Commissioner of Agriculture","d":"","vf":"1","c":[["Wilton Simpson","Republican"],["Joey Mendoza Atkins","Democratic"]],"wi":1,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"State Representative","d":"District 45","vf":"1","c":[["Erin Huntley","Republican"],["Leonard Spencer","Democratic"]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"q","title":"Retention of Justice Carlos G. Muñiz (Supreme Court)","pre":"","q":"Shall Justice Carlos G. Muñiz of the Supreme Court be retained in office?","r":["Yes","No"]},{"t":"r","title":"Circuit Judge","d":"9th Judicial Circuit, Group 1","vf":"1","c":[["Temika Hampton-Johnson",""],["Charles Hart",""]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"q","title":"No. 1 Constitutional Amendment — Budget Stabilization Fund","pre":"","q":"Proposing an amendment to the State Constitution to increase the amount of funds that may be retained in the budget stabilization fund from 10% to 25% of general revenue collections, require the legislature to transfer the lesser of $750 million or the amount required to reach 25% of the general revenue collections each year unless certain conditions are met, and allow the legislature to withdraw funds for critical state needs.","r":["Yes","No"]},{"t":"q","title":"No. 2 Constitutional Amendment — Exemption of Tangible Personal Property on Agricultural Land from Taxation","pre":"","q":"Proposing an amendment to the State Constitution to exempt tangible personal property habitually located or typically present on land classified as agricultural, used in the production of agricultural products or for agritourism activities, and owned by the landowner or leaseholder of the agricultural land from ad valorem taxation. If approved this amendment would first apply for tax years beginning January 1, 2027.","r":["Yes","No"]},{"t":"q","title":"No. 3 Constitutional Amendment — Increased Homestead Exemption; Lower Cap on Increases in Non-Homestead Property Assessments","pre":"","q":"This amendment increases the homestead exemption, for all non-school taxes, to $150,000 in 2027 and $250,000 in 2028, and adjusts for inflation thereafter. It requires the Legislature to prescribe a uniform procedure for counties and municipalities, for their respective levies, to increase the homestead exemption up to full assessed value, and allows special districts, subject to referendum approval, to do the same. Persons who are not Florida residents on December 31, 2026, will receive the existing homestead exemption upon qualifying for a homestead exemption, with the increased homestead exemption beginning with the fifth year of exemption, to the extent permitted by the U.S. Constitution. This amendment reduces the annual cap on assessment increases for non-homestead properties from 10% to 5%. This amendment requires counties and municipalities to use property taxes solely for public safety, education and schools, infrastructure, natural resources, bond debt service, retirement benefits for employees, and operations and administration. Other expenditures may be approved by county officers or county or municipal governing bodies unless prohibited by general law, notwithstanding Article VII, Section 9(a) of the Florida Constitution, which allows counties and municipalities to levy property taxes for their respective purposes. This amendment takes effect January 1, 2027.","r":["Yes","No"]},{"t":"q","title":"Osceola County School Board Referendum — Funding Essential School Operating Expenses Through a One Mill Ad Valorem Tax Levy","pre":"","q":"To provide for essential operating expenses, including competitive compensation and benefits to recruit and retain high quality teachers and staff, maintain safety and security personnel, preserve academic programs, arts, music, athletics and student activities, shall the School District of Osceola County levy an ad valorem tax of one mill for four years, to be shared proportionately between public and charter schools, with oversight by an independent citizen advisory committee?","r":["Yes","No"]},{"t":"r","title":"Representative in Congress","d":"District 9","vf":"1","c":[["Dan Green","Republican"],["Darren Soto","Democratic"]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"State Representative","d":"District 46","vf":"1","c":[["Michael Cruz","Republican"],["Jose Alvarez","Democratic"],["Ivan A. Rivera","No Party Affiliation"]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"City of Kissimmee City Commissioner","d":"Seat 4","vf":"1","c":[["Tiffany Jeffers",""],["Janette Martinez",""]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"Reunion East Community Development District","d":"Seat 5","vf":"1","c":[["Diana Boyce",""],["Jill Mulhere",""]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"County Commissioner","d":"District 2","vf":"1","c":[["Olga Gonzalez","Republican"],["Viviana Janer","Democratic"]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"VillaSol Community Development District","d":"Seat 1","vf":"1","c":[["Mario A. Cordova",""],["Timothy Gagnon",""]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"VillaSol Community Development District","d":"Seat 4","vf":"1","c":[["Servando \"Junior\" Comas",""],["Corey T. Gagnon",""]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"VillaSol Community Development District","d":"Seat 5","vf":"1","c":[["Ramon E. Bermudez",""],["Herman Perez",""]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"Concorde Estates Community Development District","d":"Seat 1","vf":"1","c":[["Joselynn Colon",""],["Jim Turner",""]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"Concorde Estates Community Development District","d":"Seat 2","vf":"1","c":[["Zahira Colls López de Victoria",""],["Victor Cruz",""],["Robin McNeil",""]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"Concorde Estates Community Development District","d":"Seat 3","vf":"1","c":[["Cesar Goyetche",""],["Aidee M. Velez",""]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"State Representative","d":"District 35","vf":"1","c":[["Erika Booth","Republican"],["Eric Gray","Democratic"]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"County Commissioner","d":"District 4","vf":"1","c":[["Donald Shroyer","Republican"],["Mary Downey","Democratic"]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"City of St. Cloud City Council Member","d":"Seat 5","vf":"1","c":[["Alex Rodriguez",""],["Kirk Zilke",""]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"Town of Kindred Community Development District","d":"Seat 3","vf":"1","c":[["Jose L. Albarran",""],["Antonio Aponte",""]],"wi":0,"note":[]},{"t":"r","title":"An